WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.593 --> 00:00:17.098
Zann saw Perda's anxious look and felt even more anxious himself.

2
00:00:17.778 --> 00:00:18.939
Mellis stepped closer.

3
00:00:18.959 --> 00:00:21.800
"Your arm looks painful," she said.

4
00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:25.361
"The entire village council is meeting at my house today.

5
00:00:26.182 --> 00:00:27.962
I can take you there to see Zira.

6
00:00:28.603 --> 00:00:29.963
Her potions will heal you."

7
00:00:29.983 --> 00:00:31.924
"Great! Let's go."

8
00:00:32.752 --> 00:00:34.913
Zann whistled for Zing, who flew over.

9
00:00:35.653 --> 00:00:36.693
Mellis looked worried.

10
00:00:36.713 --> 00:00:39.354
"Perhaps we should leave your pet behind.

11
00:00:40.094 --> 00:00:43.215
Zira is the most accomplished scientist in this part of Terrica.

12
00:00:43.695 --> 00:00:48.056
If she hasn't seen such a beast before, she might want to study him further."

13
00:00:48.076 --> 00:00:51.897
"Mellis doesn't believe we're from another world," Zann thought.

14
00:00:52.518 --> 00:00:55.218
What if Zira and the other adults felt the same way?

15
00:00:55.898 --> 00:00:58.259
Then again, what if they did believe them?

16
00:00:59.179 --> 00:01:00.880
Zira might want to study them too!

17
00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.322
"We probably shouldn't mention where we're from," he said to Perda.

18
00:01:05.903 --> 00:01:07.784
"We could tie Zing to that tree to wait for us."

19
00:01:08.604 --> 00:01:12.927
Zing let out an angry whistle and shot a puff of steam in Zann's face.

20
00:01:12.947 --> 00:01:15.089
"That tiny tree?

21
00:01:15.709 --> 00:01:20.353
He'd yank it right out of the ground if he doesn't feel like staying," Perda said.

22
00:01:20.373 --> 00:01:22.954
"Maybe we could disguise him somehow."

23
00:01:23.795 --> 00:01:24.936
Mellis looked thoughtful.

24
00:01:24.956 --> 00:01:28.118
"He's about the same size as a chupo."

25
00:01:28.138 --> 00:01:29.719
"What's a chupo?"

26
00:01:30.139 --> 00:01:30.800
Zann asked.

27
00:01:31.592 --> 00:01:33.113
"A creature that lives in the mountains."

28
00:01:33.833 --> 00:01:36.974
Mellis pointed toward the mountain range Zann had noticed earlier.

29
00:01:36.994 --> 00:01:41.256
"Chupos are pretty rare since they're a favorite snack of rock trompers."

30
00:01:42.076 --> 00:01:42.697
She shuddered.

31
00:01:43.457 --> 00:01:44.517
"Rock trompers?"

32
00:01:44.997 --> 00:01:45.698
Perda echoed.

33
00:01:45.718 --> 00:01:51.140
"Yes. They're terrifying and dangerous creatures that also live in the mountains."

34
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.481
Mellis looked at Zing again.

35
00:01:53.501 --> 00:01:58.203
"Everyone has heard of chupos, but few in this area have seen one.

36
00:01:58.943 --> 00:02:03.745
Let's see if we can turn your, um, dragon into a chupo."

37
00:02:07.128 --> 00:02:10.950
First Mellis said they had to hide Zing's gleaming red scales.

38
00:02:11.551 --> 00:02:16.014
She had a bottle of water in her rough cloth bag, and the kids mixed it with dirt

39
00:02:16.074 --> 00:02:17.535
to create a muddy paste.

40
00:02:18.635 --> 00:02:21.497
Zing wasn't happy about having mud rubbed on him.

41
00:02:22.058 --> 00:02:26.160
Zann was glad that he couldn't shoot fire at the moment, only hot steam.

42
00:02:26.901 --> 00:02:29.242
Even so, it was difficult to keep him still.

43
00:02:29.262 --> 00:02:34.250
"I wish Darb were here," he muttered, dodging a slap from Zing's wing.

44
00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:36.912
"He can convince Zing to do almost anything."

45
00:02:37.672 --> 00:02:38.433
Perda nodded.

46
00:02:38.453 --> 00:02:40.254
"Hold still, Zing.

47
00:02:40.454 --> 00:02:41.355
We missed a spot."

48
00:02:41.975 --> 00:02:45.357
Finally Zing was the same drab color as the landscape.

49
00:02:45.377 --> 00:02:47.759
"Chupos don't have wings though."

50
00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:49.821
Mellis studied the dragon.

51
00:02:49.841 --> 00:02:53.803
"And you can still tell he's covered in scales, not fur."

52
00:02:54.804 --> 00:02:56.705
Perda glanced at Mellis' bag.

53
00:02:56.725 --> 00:03:00.368
"Maybe we could wrap him in that," she suggested.

54
00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:03.561
"We could say he's injured, and it's a bandage."

55
00:03:04.401 --> 00:03:05.181
"Good idea!"

56
00:03:05.941 --> 00:03:08.102
Mellis dumped a few items out of the bag.

57
00:03:08.742 --> 00:03:12.643
Then she pulled off the rope belt that cinched in her loose tunic.

58
00:03:12.663 --> 00:03:15.104
"We can use this to tie it on him."

59
00:03:16.864 --> 00:03:19.245
Soon Zing was fully disguised.

60
00:03:20.025 --> 00:03:22.246
Zann wasn't sure what a chupo looked like.

61
00:03:22.806 --> 00:03:26.927
But he doubted it looked like a dragon covered in mud and draped in a bag.

62
00:03:26.947 --> 00:03:30.548
"Let's hope nobody looks too closely," Mellis said.

63
00:03:31.104 --> 00:03:32.184
"It's the best we can do.

64
00:03:32.865 --> 00:03:34.805
Follow me—the farm is this way."

65
00:03:37.746 --> 00:03:42.907
Zing's legs and wings were restricted by the bag so the kids took turns carrying him.

66
00:03:42.927 --> 00:03:45.328
"How far away is your house?"

67
00:03:45.808 --> 00:03:48.569
Zann asked after they'd been walking for several minutes.

68
00:03:48.589 --> 00:03:53.190
"At our current pace, we should be there within an hour," Mellis replied.

69
00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:56.431
Zann and Perda traded a dismayed glance.

70
00:03:56.451 --> 00:04:01.220
"I wish we had enough magic to create more comfortable shoes," Zann said.

71
00:04:01.881 --> 00:04:03.002
Perda rolled her eyes.

72
00:04:03.022 --> 00:04:07.904
"If we had magic, we wouldn't need better shoes," she reminded him.

73
00:04:07.924 --> 00:04:09.986
"We'd just zap there!"

74
00:04:10.786 --> 00:04:12.907
Zann shifted his grip on Zing.

75
00:04:13.568 --> 00:04:16.329
The little dragon felt heavier with every step.

76
00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:20.212
Mellis distracted the visitors by telling them more about herself.

77
00:04:20.792 --> 00:04:24.194
She'd lost both her parents to a famine when she was very young.

78
00:04:24.835 --> 00:04:29.830
Her uncle Vilkor had taken her in, and now the two of them eked out a living on

79
00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:31.612
their large but arid farm.

80
00:04:31.632 --> 00:04:36.156
"It's not easy," she admitted with a sigh.

81
00:04:36.176 --> 00:04:39.338
"Especially now that our main well has run dry.

82
00:04:39.939 --> 00:04:41.900
That's why I was out there when you arrived.

83
00:04:42.581 --> 00:04:45.063
Uncle Vilkor had sent me to dig a new well."

84
00:04:45.784 --> 00:04:48.005
Zann was amazed by Mellis' tale.

85
00:04:48.726 --> 00:04:51.328
Life without magic sounded really difficult!

86
00:04:52.469 --> 00:04:55.492
Finally they spotted a few buildings on the horizon.

87
00:04:56.120 --> 00:05:02.205
There was a small barn, a separate building for storing dried grains, and a modest one-story house.

88
00:05:03.166 --> 00:05:04.867
Three people were sitting in the yard.

89
00:05:05.588 --> 00:05:11.012
By now Zann was so exhausted from the long walk that he barely took in the names when

90
00:05:11.052 --> 00:05:12.153
Mellis introduced them.

91
00:05:12.894 --> 00:05:17.857
Uncle Vilkor was tall and handsome, with a big smile and a strong handshake.

92
00:05:17.878 --> 00:05:21.500
"Welcome, welcome," he said.

93
00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:25.404
"Visitors from far away—what fun!"

94
00:05:26.628 --> 00:05:31.149
Then there was a man named Krub, who was broad-shouldered and rough-looking.

95
00:05:32.030 --> 00:05:36.591
He didn't say much, but when he did speak, his voice was loud and gruff.

96
00:05:38.531 --> 00:05:44.173
Finally Mellis introduced Zira, a small, lean woman with steely gray eyes.

97
00:05:44.193 --> 00:05:48.794
"Let's have a look," Zira said, examining Zann's scrape.

98
00:05:49.514 --> 00:05:51.455
"Yes, this should be a simple matter.

99
00:05:52.315 --> 00:05:55.596
Let's go indoors so the dust doesn't contaminate my potion.

100
00:05:56.340 --> 00:05:59.101
It's quite rare and difficult to make, you know."

101
00:05:59.881 --> 00:06:01.362
She sounded proud of her work.

102
00:06:02.222 --> 00:06:04.122
Soon Zann found out why.

103
00:06:04.823 --> 00:06:10.144
The moment Zira rubbed her purple paste-like potion onto his wound, it stopped hurting.

104
00:06:10.164 --> 00:06:11.965
"Wow, thanks!"

105
00:06:12.385 --> 00:06:12.765
he said.

106
00:06:13.565 --> 00:06:17.286
Then he noticed Krub watching Zing with narrowed eyes.

107
00:06:17.906 --> 00:06:22.128
None of the adults had paid much attention to the dragon when Mellis had said he was an

108
00:06:22.228 --> 00:06:23.048
injured chupo.

109
00:06:23.564 --> 00:06:29.109
But now Zing was nosing at the fire in the hearth, obviously trying to figure out how to

110
00:06:29.169 --> 00:06:30.230
regain his powers.

111
00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:32.351
"What's the chupo doing?"

112
00:06:32.752 --> 00:06:34.733
Krub said, sounding suspicious.

113
00:06:34.753 --> 00:06:38.657
"Nothing." Mellis grabbed Zing.

114
00:06:38.677 --> 00:06:43.241
"Er, Uncle, our guests are tired from their long trip.

115
00:06:43.961 --> 00:06:45.903
Shall we show them to their beds?"
